    "runtime_settings": {
      "CUDA_HOME": "<environment>/site-packages/nvidia/cuda_nvcc, so jaxlib assembles the bridge's Triton PTX with the locked CUDA 12.9 ptxas instead of a node's system toolkit",
      "XLA_FLAGS": "--xla_gpu_enable_command_buffer= (the Triton custom-call bridge runs outside command buffers)",
      "EJKERNEL_TRITON_CACHE_DIR": "<artifact_root>/.cache/gla_key_dimension/triton",
      "TRANSFORMER_HOST_STAGING": "0 (direct H100 transfers)"
    },
    "attention_backend": "fused (chunked Triton), pinned in every recipe",
    "acceptance": "per GPU type and source/config/runtime identity: GLA CPU tests, fused-kernel GPU tests, initialization hash, 20-update full-recipe pilot, and exact fresh-process resume at update 21",
    "kernel_operands": "Q, K, V, and the output cotangent enter the Triton kernels as FP32. With BF16 operands upcast in-kernel, Triton 3.6 on sm_103 (B300) ran FP32 IEEE products at TF32-level precision (4e-4 relative output error vs 1e-7 on H100); FP32 operands fix this without changing the arithmetic.",
